issues.body:
Not started. From docs/plan/native-modern-game.md Phase 7:

- pre-battle, help and militia redistribution - these still pass through the legacy map screen (deliberately left there by PR #20, drawn via PassThrough);
- auto-resolve (a readable battle panel);
- shopkeeper (trade UI with a grid and comparisons);
- merc hiring and contract flows;
- end-game screens and the intro/ending presentation;
- editor decision: keep the legacy editor or rebuild it later (not player facing).

Follow M1-M4 per screen: functional spec, wireframes approved by the owner, build, parity tour + layout audit + screenshots. One PR per screen.
Milestone: Native modern: remaining screens.

## Todo

- [x] pre-battle, help and militia redistribution (legacy map screen PassThrough today)
- [x] auto-resolve - a readable battle panel (PR #90)
- [x] shopkeeper - trade UI with a grid and comparisons
- [x] merc hiring and contract flows
- [x] end-game screens and the intro/ending presentation - the native intro/ending cinema and the new victory epilogue (PR #279)
- [x] editor decision: keep the legacy editor or rebuild it later (not player facing)

HD content art per the asset methodology in docs/plan/native-modern-game.md. Generated on the player's machine from their own game files, never committed (licensing decision, PR #12).

Order by usage:
1. merc faces - upscale + cleanup, hand repaint for the most-seen mercs;
2. item pictures (small and big);
3. world tiles by tileset, then animations - palette swaps keep working through recolour masks, tile seams and frame stability are gated;
4. load screens, radar maps (regenerated from data) and optional video.

Tooling and gates exist: tools/assets/, assets/manifest.json (7,615 assets classified). World art follows Phase 8 (done); faces and items can start now. Each batch is its own PR with comparison sheets.
Milestone: Native modern: HD art + legacy removal.

Last phase, after every screen is native (docs/plan/native-modern-game.md Phase 10):

- delete the legacy UI screen code;
- delete the 640x480 layout helpers (STD_SCREEN_*, anchor shims);
- delete the UI blitter path and the legacy golden images;
- decide whether the software world renderer is still needed as a fallback;
- simplify Video.cc.

Milestone: Native modern: HD art + legacy removal.

Two gaps from PR #19:

- no live-explosion scene in the equivalence test (translucent overlays and outlines under motion are untested);
- the driven-window screenshots are composed from the read-back world with nearest scaling, while a player sees SDL's pixel-art filter - the proof does not match what ships.

Placeholder goal, not yet planned: make the AI measurably better and data-driven on both layers, without changing what the rules mean.

Tactical layer (src/game/Tactical AI: AI.cc, AIInternals, IsolateSight, morale/energy):
- audit and document what the 1999 rules actually do (an M1-style functional spec);
- externalize the tunables to src/externalized/ JSON so behaviour can be changed without a recompile;
- put the known unfairness (cheating, Omni sight) behind explicit difficulty settings instead of removing it silently;
- new behaviours only where the rules allow: cover evaluation, suppression, grenade use, retreat and regroup.

Strategic layer (Strategic/ enemy movement, StrategicAI, mines and income, reinforcements, air control):
- audit and spec, externalize the priorities, make enemy offensives legible to the player;
- deterministic and seeded so a scenario replays.

Guardrails: same-game rule (campaign data and saves keep their meaning), every change covered by the tactical battle e2e track, nothing pushed upstream.
First task: write docs/plan/ai-modernization.md - nothing under this track starts before that exists.

﻿Follow-up from #171 (Phase 6 native laptop). `tests/e2e/laptop_parity.lua` stops at the M.E.R.C. home page: it never opens an account or hires.

Done when:
- the parity tour opens an account (`LaptopNative::MercOpenAccount`), opens the files page and hires a merc (`LaptopNative::MercHire`), asserting the account status, the team, the balance and the daily cost against game state;
- it covers the no-account gate and, when reachable with the test aids, the server-down broken link;
- `ctest -L e2e` and the resolution matrix stay green.

Reference: `docs/ui/laptop.md` section 4.7, section 9.

﻿Follow-up from #171 (Phase 6 native laptop). `tests/e2e/laptop_parity.lua` stops at the personality quiz; the rest of the flow is not exercised.

Done when:
- the parity tour drives quiz -> attributes -> portrait -> voice -> finish -> confirm through the native pages;
- it asserts the created profile (name, nickname, stats, portrait, voice, skills), the $3,000 charge and the character's arrival, against game state;
- `LaptopNative::ImpCreate` is covered including the no-funds and invalid gate results.

Reference: `docs/ui/laptop.md` section 4.8, section 9.

﻿Follow-up from #171 (Phase 6 native laptop). The parity tour only calls a merc who is available; the answering-machine path is not covered.

Done when:
- the tour calls a merc who is away, asserts the answering-machine state and the pre-recorded quote;
- Leave message sets `PROFILE_MISC_FLAG3_PLAYER_LEFT_MSG_FOR_MERC_AT_AIM` and the merc mails back later (assert the mail/flag);
- the refuse path (hated merc / death rate / morale) is asserted too, if reachable with test aids.

Reference: `docs/ui/laptop.md` section 4.6, section 9.

﻿The plan's cross-cutting localisation: the native laptop strings ship in English only and the long-translation layout audit has not run.

Done when:
- the resolution/layout tours run with the German, Russian and Polish string tables loaded;
- any clipped, overlapping or truncated text on the native laptop is fixed (or carries an explicit ellipsis/tooltip);
- the audit is wired into CI or the release checklist.

Reference: `docs/plan/native-modern-game.md` (Cross-cutting concerns, Localisation), `docs/ui/laptop.md` section 7.

﻿Several native laptop pages are plain wrapped-text lists rather than the design-system layouts used elsewhere: the mortuary, the I.M.P. home/about-us, and the A.I.M. policies/history/links/alumni pages (the legacy alumni page shows faces and bios).

Done when:
- those pages use the design-system section/table/card patterns like the rest of the laptop;
- the A.I.M. alumni page shows the faces and bios from the AIM listing data, not just names;
- the letter/authorship of the legacy text data is preserved.

Reference: `docs/ui/laptop.md` sections 4.6, 4.8, 4.12.

﻿The native laptop (#171) draws fewer incidental random numbers than the legacy UI during the same scripted flow. That shifts later random merc quotes and the selected merc, so `mapscreen_parity/mapscreen_log.png`, `map_screen_tour/map.png`, `autoresolve_parity/autoresolve_result.png` and `menus_tour/autoresolve.png` were regenerated even though those screens did not change.

Done when:
- the campaign step framework reseeds the RNG at defined flow points (new game, entering the map, staging a battle) so a UI change cannot churn unrelated goldens;
- the seeded determinism check still passes;
- the affected strategic-map/auto-resolve goldens no longer depend on the laptop path.

Reference: PR #171, `docs/plan/e2e-tactical-battles.md`, `docs/plan/e2e-screen-automation.md`.
